.TH STREAMTAIL 1 "May 21, 2026" "streamtail 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
streamtail \- follow changing HTTP content like tail -f for URLs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B streamtail
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " URL"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B streamtail
polls an HTTP or HTTPS URL, keeps a snapshot of the previous response body,
and writes only newly appended response text to standard output.
.PP
It is intended for terminal and pipe workflows where a remote endpoint behaves
like an append-only log, status feed, or simple text stream.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-method " " \fIMETHOD\fR
HTTP method to use. The default is
.BR GET ,
or
.B POST
when
.BR \-\-body
is provided without an explicit method.
.TP
.BR \-\-body " " \fITEXT\fR
Request body to send.
.TP
.BR \-\-header " " \fINAME:VALUE\fR
Add an HTTP header. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-user-agent " " \fIVALUE\fR
Set the HTTP User-Agent header.
.TP
.BR \-\-proxy " " \fIURL\fR
Send requests through an HTTP or HTTPS proxy.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fIDURATION\fR
Polling interval. Durations support suffixes such as
.BR ms ,
.BR s ,
.BR m ,
and
.BR h .
The default interval is 2s.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fIDURATION\fR
HTTP timeout per request. The default timeout is 10s.
.TP
.BR \-\-max-retries " " \fIN|unlimited\fR
Maximum number of consecutive retryable failures before exiting. The default is
.BR unlimited .
.TP
.BR \-\-retry-status " " \fICODE\fR
Retry an additional HTTP status code. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-once
Fetch once, print the initial body, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow-from-end
Start after the first fetched snapshot. This behaves more like
.BR tail " " \-f
for endpoints that already contain historical content.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emit each update as a JSON Lines record with a
.B data
field.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fICOLOR\fR
Color text output written to standard output. Supported colors are
.BR black ,
.BR red ,
.BR green ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR blue ,
.BR magenta ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR white ,
and their
.B bright-
variants. Color formatting is not written to output files.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-color
Disable terminal color formatting.
.TP
.BR \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Write stream output to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-\-append-output
Append stream output to the file selected with
.BR \-\-output
instead of replacing it. This option requires
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.BR \-\-exit-on-match " " \fIREGEX\fR
Exit successfully after emitted output matches a regular expression.
.TP
.BR \-\-max-events " " \fIN\fR
Exit successfully after emitting
.I N
updates.
.TP
.BR \-\-max-duration " " \fIDURATION\fR
Exit successfully after the total runtime reaches the duration.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Write debug logging to the file selected with
.BR \-\-log .
This option requires
.BR \-\-log .
.TP
.BR \-\-log " " \fIPATH\fR
Debug log output file.
.TP
.BR \-\-ca-cert " " \fIPATH\fR
Add PEM or DER CA certificate roots for TLS verification.
.TP
.BR \-\-insecure
Disable TLS certificate verification. This is intended only for local testing
or trusted internal networks.
.TP
.BR \-\-basic-auth " " \fIUSER:PASSWORD\fR
Send HTTP Basic authentication credentials.
.TP
.BR \-\-token " " \fITOKEN\fR
Send bearer token authentication in the Authorization header.
.TP
.BR \-\-token-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Read bearer token authentication from a file. Leading and trailing whitespace is
trimmed.
.TP
.BR \-\-token-env " " \fINAME\fR
Read bearer token authentication from an environment variable.
.TP
.BR \-\-netrc
Use matching Basic authentication credentials from
.BR ~/.netrc .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure, such as a non-retryable HTTP response or output error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Follow a URL:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs
.TP
Poll every two seconds:
.B streamtail https://example.com/api/events --interval 2s
.TP
Fetch once:
.B streamtail https://example.com/ --once
.TP
Emit JSON Lines:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --json
.TP
Use Basic authentication:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --basic-auth user:pass
.TP
Use bearer token authentication:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --token "$STREAMTAIL_TOKEN"
.TP
Use bearer token authentication from the environment:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --token-env STREAMTAIL_TOKEN
.TP
Use matching .netrc credentials:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --netrc
.TP
Write debug logs:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --debug --log streamtail.log
.TP
Color terminal output:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --color cyan
.TP
Start from the current end and save output:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs -f --header "X-Env: prod" --output logs.txt
.TP
Append output to an existing file:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --output logs.txt --append-output
.TP
Exit when output matches:
.B streamtail https://example.com/logs --exit-on-match "deploy complete"
.TP
Send a POST body:
.B streamtail https://example.com/query --method POST --body '{"service":"api"}'
.TP
Use a custom CA certificate:
.B streamtail https://internal.example/logs --ca-cert ./internal-ca.pem
.SH NOTES
HTTP 5xx responses and transport failures are retryable. HTTP 401 and 403
responses are fatal unless explicitly selected with
.BR \-\-retry-status .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tail (1),
.BR curl (1)
